  ],
  "notes": "From English \"dial.\" Can be used as a noun for the physical control or with する as a verb meaning to dial a number.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ダイヤルを{回|まわ}す: to turn the dial\n- ダイヤルする: to dial (a number)\n- ダイヤル{式|しき}{電話|でんわ}: rotary phone\n- {音量|おんりょう}のダイヤル: volume dial\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ボタン: button — press, not rotate\n- つまみ: knob — native term, often used for radio/oven controls",
